      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 511362484,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I was surprised that no other dissector does something similar to what I'm trying in this patch.\n\nUsing http(s), we can also download a file of any type. It seems that we use the \"opposite approach\" in this case: File types have to register themselves as potential http payloads.\n\nWhat is the recommended way to say \"dissect this blob as a file if you can figure out the file type\"?",
